======================================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE BRACKET: pin the baryonic part by the design target, reduce the gap to ONE inequality.
======================================================================================================================

  The design target is H_SS=-3 at S=0.1 on the FLAT-VACUUM design point (R~0).  With R~0 there, the closed
  form gives the baryonic constant:  -e^{0.1} P0 = -3  =>  P0 = 3 e^{-0.1} = 2.7145.
  In a galaxy S=(2-u)Phi is a weak-field potential (Phi ~ 1e-6), so e^{S} ~ 1 and the baryonic part is -P0.
  Then H_SS(galaxy, r) = -P0 - v(S) R(r), and health (L72's window) is H_SS in (-5.294, 0):
      UPPER (<0):   -P0 - v R < 0    <=>   v R > -P0   -- ALWAYS true (v R >= 0).           [curvature-safe]
      LOWER (>M*):  -P0 - v R > M*   <=>   v R < -M* - P0 = 5.294 - 2.7145 = 2.580.         [the ONE bound]

    P0 (pinned by design H_SS=-3 at R~0) = 2.7145
    baryonic H_SS(galaxy) = -P0 = -2.7145  (interior to (-5.294,0), c_IR = 0.4350 > 0)
    HEALTH HOLDS  <=>  v(S) R  <  -M* - P0 = 2.5791   (reduced, dimensionless)
  [PASS] BRACKET-1  the baryonic H_SS(galaxy) = -P0 = -2.71 is INTERIOR to the healthy window with c_IR = 0.4350 > 0: with zero curvature the galactic scalar is HEALTHY.  So the entire question is what the curvature term does   (-P0=-2.7145 in (-5.294,0))
  [PASS] BRACKET-2  [THE DELIVERABLE] the galactic propagating scalar is healthy  <=>  v(S) R < 2.58 (dimensionless, reduced) at every radius.  This SINGLE falsifiable inequality on ONE calibration number REPLACES L71's 'underspecified, cannot be certified either way'.  Positive headroom exists (2.58 > 0), so a healthy calibration is NOT excluded; the floor is only reached if the reduced curvature exceeds 2.58 near r_M   (headroom to floor = 2.5791 reduced units (both footings share it: window & P0 are footing-free))
  [PASS] BRACKET-3  the bound is FOOTING-INDEPENDENT: M*, P0, v(S) and the window are all built from dimensionless design coefficients, and a_0 enters only through the (uncalibrated) map to the reduced R -- so the 2.58 target is identical on canonical and alt footings   (both footings: same 2.58 reduced-unit target; footing enters only via astra's unfixed length calibration)

